    "detail": "Exact source snapshot hits reuse the published artifact. When the root and build assumptions match but a resolved module source hash changes, a fresh valid Stage-0 semantic check computes the canonical root and resolved-module semantic identity; the verified VM artifact is reused only if that identity and the typed callable interface still match. A comment-only imported-module edit took 0.183 s and reused the artifact, while a semantic dependency change took 0.384 s and rebuilt; the reused artifact result matched the independent Stage-0 oracle. A changed root function or dependency semantic value still recomputes source checking, SSA verification, and artifact generation. Function-level and independently verified module-fact reuse remain unimplemented, so Gate B is partial. A byte-distinct compiler-probe executable changed the cache key, forced a miss and recomputed source checking, SSA verification, and the VM artifact; the newly built artifact produced a result equal to the independent Stage-0 oracle.",
